  "name": "14 St-Union Sq",
  "approximate": true,
  "notes": [
    "Frame: bearing 90, so u = meters east of the anchor (40.735, -73.9902) and v = meters south. Every point was computed in this frame from the pinned OSM vertices and Open Data entrance points.",
    "Station complex 602: 635 (IRT Lexington Av), L03 (BMT Canarsie), R20 (BMT Broadway). Layout facts from English Wikipedia '14th Street–Union Square station', revision 1382952620 (2026-10-31), facts only: the Lexington and Broadway platforms are two levels below ground; the Canarsie station crosses under both along 14 St; a 480 ft mezzanine above the Broadway platforms ramps down to a control area at its south end; a 20 ft corridor from there slopes down to the IRT mezzanine; two overpasses above the IRT platforms, with galleries and stairs down to each island; a corridor above the west side of the IRT joins the overpasses; a stair from the IRT mezzanine to a small mezzanine above the Canarsie platform; a western Canarsie mezzanine whose passages to the Broadway concourse are sealed; one stair from the south end of each Broadway platform to the Canarsie platform; an escalator from the Canarsie platform to the IRT mezzanine; no elevators to the Lexington platforms.",
    "Levels from E&E rises: mezzanine -3.82 m = EL217 12'-6 1/4in (street to the Lexington mezzanine); platforms-upper -6.92 m = that plus EL220 10'-2in (mezzanine to the downtown Broadway platform; EL219's '10in- 2in' read as the same rise); platform-canarsie -11.86 m = mezzanine plus EL218 26'-4 1/2in (3 landings).",
    "UNVERIFIED: one mezzanine level stands for all of them. The Broadway mezzanine is shallower than the IRT one (the corridor slopes down to it), the small mezzanine above the Canarsie platform may sit lower, and Wikipedia gives the Broadway platforms 30 ft below the street, deeper than the E&E-derived -6.92 m.",
    "UNVERIFIED: the Lexington platforms share the Broadway platforms' level. No E&E rise reaches them; OSM tags both at level -2 and Wikipedia puts both two levels below ground.",
    "Tracks: one per stop, the OSM subway way (catalog/osm-tracks.json) where it lies within 4.5 m of its platform and 5 m of the map's line for its direction: L03N 808580928, L03S 552261294, 635N 813742875 (uptown local), 635S 817018810 (downtown express; the downtown local way runs about 10 m off the map's S line), R20N 813742876, R20S 817415213. The other tracks are not drawn.",
    "UNVERIFIED: mezzanine outlines. Drawn to contain every connector end and to follow the Wikipedia description (the IRT overpasses at about v -24..-4 and 54..74, galleries over each island, the west corridor, the small mezzanine over the Canarsie platform folded into mezz-lexington); real extents unknown. All three slabs are marked approximate.",
    "UNVERIFIED: IRT platform stairs (OSM 509025003-509025012, level -2;-1, MTA stair numbers in their descriptions): the top is taken as the end toward the nearer overpass.",
    "UNVERIFIED: Broadway platform stairs (OSM 509025019-509025028) come in pairs whose flights meet at their tops.",
    "L to Broadway stairs st-509025053 and st-509025055 (OSM level -3;-2): both ends at the OSM ways' end vertices; each way bends once and is drawn straight.",
    "UNVERIFIED: Canarsie platform stairs. OSM maps only their top flights (509025049, 509025050, 509025051, 509025061, 509025062, level -2;-1). The top stays on the OSM vertex and the foot is extended along the way onto the island, 14 m (11 m for 509025051, which would otherwise reach 509025050's top), so the 8 m rise is drawable. Which end is the top is a guess: 509025049 and 509025061 rise toward each other, 509025050 and 509025051 east toward the IRT mezzanine, 509025062 south toward 14 St (its foot crosses over the L03S track onto the island; the OSM way ends 0.8 m outside the platform polygon).",
    "UNVERIFIED: ES219 has no OSM way. Its run is 14 m along the north side of the island, rising east to beside EL218; the E&E point is at the island's south edge. Direction up, from the E&E text.",
    "EL217: the E&E row has no notes and its lat/lon is at Columbus Circle. Placed at OSM elevator node 7668123469 (level -1;0) in the Zeckendorf Towers and listed by the Zeckendorf 14 St easement entrance (Wikipedia: an elevator in the Zeckendorf Towers entrance at 4 Av and 14 St).",
    "EL218, EL219, EL220: at the centroids of their OSM elevator ways (509025052, 509025029, 509025030).",
    "ES257X, ES258X: the E&E points are next to the Zeckendorf 14 St easement entrance; placed at it with no run of their own (the renderer gives them one).",
    "Street stairs: tops are the Open Data entrance points, feet the other end of each OSM way. UNVERIFIED: 509025048's incline tag makes the end away from the entrance its top; that end is used as the foot anyway (the other end is 1.9 m from the entrance). 1112132922 and 1112170143 (16 St park stairs) have no level tag; their 17 steps suggest a rise near 3.1 m, less than the -3.82 m mezzanine.",
    "UNVERIFIED: st-4av-sw-1 (entrance e-4av-sw-1) has no OSM way: drawn parallel to st-509025059 along 14 St, a 5.5 m run descending west.",
    "Not used: OSM steps 509025063 and 509025064 (level -1;0, no Open Data entrance: the closed exit on the west side of Broadway between 13 and 14 St, Wikipedia), 509024997 (one level), and the untagged park landscaping steps.",
    "UNVERIFIED: walk-bmt-irt stands for the 20 ft corridor. Its ends are guesses at the Broadway control area's east edge and the IRT north overpass's west end; it is drawn flat on the one mezzanine level.",
    "UNVERIFIED: widths. Street stairs 1.5 m, IRT and Broadway platform stairs 1.8 m, Canarsie stairs 2.4 m.",
    "UNVERIFIED: entrance ids name corners from the Wikipedia exit list and the frame; which of a corner's two stairs is -1 or -2 is arbitrary.",
    "No fare control lines and no paid flags: positions unknown."
  ],
